inkrs-afv

Inference for Qual's AFV fibre model V2 (https://huggingface.co/Qualzz20/afv_fiber_9um_v2). The model, its
architecture and its normalisation are Qual's: inkrs-afv ships none of them and runs the model.py of the snapshot
you point it at.

Its tiling, padding, blend ramp, softmax, quantisation, tracing downsample and, in --mode villa, its choice of tiles
and output chunks follow villa's lasagna.qualzz_inference and lasagna.tiled_predict3d
(https://github.com/ScrollPrize/villa, commit 97fb9336c). inkrs_afv/contract.py's blend_ramp is copied from
lasagna/tiled_predict3d.py, and inkrs_afv/villa.py reimplements villa's tile-selection rule. villa is MIT licensed,
